cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use SegFusionFormer in your research, please cite this software repository."

type: software

title: "SegFusionFormer: Segmentation-Guided Explainable Hybrid CNN–Transformer Framework for Multi-Label Thoracic Disease Classification"

authors:
  - given-names: "Solomon"
    family-names: "Rajan P"

repository-code: "https://github.com/solomonrajannadar/SegFusionFormer"

abstract: >
  SegFusionFormer is a segmentation-guided explainable
  hybrid CNN–Transformer research framework for
  multi-label thoracic disease classification from
  chest radiographs. It integrates U-Net lung
  segmentation, mask-guided attention, EfficientNet-B0,
  MaxViT-Tiny, adaptive feature fusion, and Grad-CAM
  explainability.

keywords:
  - Deep Learning
  - Medical Imaging
  - Chest X-ray
  - Thoracic Disease Classification
  - CNN
  - Vision Transformer
  - U-Net
  - Explainable AI
  - SegFusionFormer